# A loop can be one sentence. it is the latest value. them is the latest list.
# Each example is its own function so the sentence ends with the function.
# Running returns 6.

To Added, given a start which is an integer, returning an integer
    the total is the start
    for each number from 1 to 3, add it to the total
    return it

To Skipped, given a start which is an integer, returning an integer
    the total is the start
    for each number from 1 to 4, add it to the total. If it is 2, skip it.
    return the total

To OtherwiseAdded, given a start which is an integer, returning an integer
    the total is the start
    for each number from 1 to 4, if it is 2, skip it, otherwise add it to the total.
    return the total

To Lengths, given a start which is an integer, returning an integer
    the notes are a list containing "a" and "bb"
    the total is the start
    for each note in the notes, add its length to the total
    return the total

To Listed, given a start which is an integer, returning an integer
    the notes are a list containing "a" and "bb"
    return the count of them plus the start

To Kept, given a start which is an integer, returning an integer
    the tally is the start
    keep increasing it until it is 3
    return it

When run, returning an integer
    the score is 0
    if (Added with 0) is equal to 6
        increase the score
    if (Skipped with 0) is equal to 10
        increase the score
    if (OtherwiseAdded with 0) is equal to 8
        increase the score
    if (Lengths with 0) is equal to 3
        increase the score
    if (Listed with 0) is equal to 2
        increase the score
    if (Kept with 0) is equal to 3
        increase the score
    give back the score
